        <div class="analysis-col">
            <p>The two at the bottom are the encouraging ones. Almost every site now has a page title and a mobile viewport tag, which were the standard complaints five years ago. That problem largely solved itself, because the platforms people build on started doing it for them.</p>
            <p>The two at the top did not. A missing security certificate and a missing social share image are both invisible to the owner and obvious to the visitor: one puts a warning in the address bar, the other turns every link shared on WhatsApp into a grey box.</p>
        </div>
