        <div class="analysis-col">
            <p>The Gulf has the lowest rate of missing HTTPS at 32.2% and the highest rate of missing meta descriptions at 31.2%. The UK is the exact reverse: worst on security at 45.6%, best on meta descriptions at 20.1%.</p>
            <p>That is not a rounding artefact, it is a real pattern, and it says something about how the two markets built their websites. It also has a practical edge to it. If you sell website work in Britain, the security warning is the thing to lead with. In the Gulf it is the fact that Google has nothing to quote about the business.</p>
            <p>The US sample is the smallest at 305 sites and the worst on almost everything, but treat it carefully: 305 is enough to see a shape and not enough to bet on a decimal place.</p>
